From: KRdp displayless experiment <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: allow QPainter for existing-output capture too

0003 lets the QPainter virtual backend serve screencasts, but only through
streamVirtualOutput. KRdp's persistent-output mode streams an existing output,
Virtual-0, through streamWaylandOutput, which kept the OpenGL-only guard, so on a
GPU-less guest every connection failed with "Unsupported compositing type" and
KRdp closed it. Use 0003's narrower guard there as well. Window and region
capture stay OpenGL-only.

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
index 5067461..732f904 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
@@ -93,7 +93,9 @@ void ScreencastManager::streamWaylandOutput(ScreencastStreamV1Interface *wayland
                                             OutputInterface *output,
                                             ScreencastV1Interface::CursorMode mode)
 {
-    if (!isSupportedCompositingType()) {
+    // The displayless KRdp persistent-output route captures Virtual-0 through
+    // stream_output. Its QPainter path produces a shared-memory screencast.
+    if (!isSupportedVirtualOutputCompositingType()) {
         waylandStream->sendFailed(i18n("Unsupported compositing type"));
         return;
     }
